      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fine I suppose, but the only reason to package up the unicode data files was because the \"official\" ones are on the website ( https://www.unicode.org/Public/UCD/latest/ ). If using the copies from the github repo it seems like it would be better to just make a mirror of that repo and clone that? Why the extra complexity of cloning, packaging, uploading, downloading?",
      "revId": "8c594fa7ce9432b8f668ef05a83742c70dc0c2d1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
