      "writtenOn": "2023-07-24T14:34:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If libgrapheme can be configured to use a git repo instead of download the files, then I\u0027d prefer we go that route. It doesn\u0027t seem like that\u0027s the case at the moment.\n\nOf note, repackaging the files might be wise anyway due to the large size of the unicodetools git repo. It took a while (~1 minute) to sync even though I only needed comparatively few files.",
      "parentUuid": "5ba82768_a95e1a6a",
      "revId": "8c594fa7ce9432b8f668ef05a83742c70dc0c2d1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a08440ab_54e20dc6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-24T15:08:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we need to write our own BUILD.gn and BUILD.bazel for libgrapheme anyway (we cannot use its Makefile because it is a makefile and because it downloads stuff from the internets) so we can point it at whatever files we want. It\u0027s just a build step that processes these files into data. In theory we could even do that once, I think and check in those or package those up instead.",
      "parentUuid": "dbe79cbb_5482bba4",
      "revId": "8c594fa7ce9432b8f668ef05a83742c70dc0c2d1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
